%% Critical path: A business application gets a document signed (Relying application (calls the signing service)).
%% No production telemetry is available, so steps carry no p50/p99 annotations.
flowchart TD
  S1["1. Service starts, reads its PIN from an encrypted systemd credential and logs in to the token<br/><small>systemd fhsm-service.service, fhsm_service.c, service PIN credential, fhsm_token.c, fhsm_token_tpm.c, fhsm_tpm.c, TPM via tpm2 CLI, slotN.tok token file</small>"]
  S2["2. Application posts the data to be signed<br/><small>/sign (private listener), fhsm_service.c</small>"]
  S1 --> S2
  S3["3. Service checks the signing policy and request budget<br/><small>fhsm_service.c, service signing policy, service refusal budget</small>"]
  S2 --> S3
  S4["4. HSM signs with the token's private key<br/><small>fhsm_pkcs11.c, fhsm_crypto.c, fhsm_token.c</small>"]
  S3 --> S4
  S5["5. The signing event is written to the tamper-evident audit log<br/><small>fhsm_audit.c, audit log (HMAC-chained JSON lines)</small>"]
  S4 --> S5
  S6["6. Signature is returned to the application<br/><small>fhsm_service.c</small>"]
  S5 --> S6
